HolSmtLib is a library for integrating Satisfiability Modulo Theories (SMT)
solvers with the HOL theorem prover.

Files:

COPYRIGHT               Copyright notice, license and disclaimer.
CVC.sml                 Functions to invoke the cvc5 SMT solver.
Holmakefile             Makefile for Holmake (to build selftest.exe).
HolSmtLib.{sig,sml}     Entry point into HolSmtLib. Provides GENERIC_SMT_TAC
                        and derived tactics to call SMT solvers.
HolSmtScript.sml        Various theorems for HolSmtLib.
Library.sml             Common auxiliary functions, tracing.
README                  This file.
selftest.sml            HolSmtLib tests.
SmtLib_Logics.sml       SMT-LIB 2 logics.
SmtLib_Parser.sml       Parsing of SMT-LIB 2 benchmarks.
SmtLib_Theories.sml     SMT-LIB 2 theories.
SmtLib.sml              Translation of HOL terms into SMT-LIB 2 format.
SolverSpec.sml          Definition of SMT solvers.
Unittest.{sig,sml}      Unit tests for HolSmtLib.
Yices.sml               Functions to invoke the Yices SMT solver.
Z3.sml                  Functions to invoke the Z3 SMT solver.
Z3_ProformaThms.sml     Proforma theorems, used for Z3 proof reconstruction.
Z3_Proof.sml            Proof reconstruction for Z3: SML type of Z3 proofs.
Z3_ProofParser.sml      Proof reconstruction for Z3: parsing of Z3's proofs.
Z3_ProofReplay.sml      Proof reconstruction for Z3: replaying Z3's proofs in
                        HOL.

Z3 version diagnostics and CI hooks:

Z3.sml reports the configured executable and discovered Z3 version through
configured_executable, configured_version and Z3version.  Z3_SMT_Prover adds
that version data path, together with the proof command stem, to proof parse
and replay failures before raising them to HolSmtLib.

Replay diagnostics from Z3_ProofReplay.sml include the proof rule, local proof
subterm, parsed HOL conclusion and a replay-state summary of asserted
hypotheses, definition hypotheses and Z3-created variables.  Unknown proof
rules are reported by Z3_ProofParser.sml with the missing rule name and local
proof subterm.

Pull-request CI runs the PolyML expk build against the Z3 versions already
provided by the docker-ci base image: 2.19.1, 4.12.4 and 4.13.0.  The
equivalent local hook is:

  docker buildx build \
    --build-arg SML=poly \
    --build-arg Z3_VERSION=<2.19.1|4.12.4|4.13.0> \
    --build-arg CVC_VERSION=5 \
    --build-arg CSDP_VERSION=1 \
    --build-arg 'BUILDOPTS=--no-cache --expk -j4 -t' \
    -f developers/docker-ci/Dockerfile .

Further documentation can be found in the HOL Description (in
HOL/Manual/Description).
